{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ravenous-dirt-widgeon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Generic, config-driven status-map override seam\n\n## Problem / findings\n\nAn audit of the Jira reconciler bridge surfaced a live-workflow change: the REB\nJira project now has a valid **Blocked** status. Absorbing that today would\nrequire editing core rebar's hardcoded status maps, which is an anti-pattern —\ncore rebar must stay project-agnostic; a single project's workflow states must\nnever be named in shipped code.\n\n### Current state of status mapping (as found)\n\nStatus mapping is HARDCODED in three places, with no config-driven seam:\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py`\n  — `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` (outbound), `blocked -> \"In Progress\"`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py`\n  — `local_to_jira_status` (outbound, blocked -> In Progress) and\n    `jira_to_local_status` (inbound, already has `\"Blocked\": \"blocked\"`).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py`\n  — `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS` (inbound, already has `\"Blocked\": \"blocked\"`) plus\n    `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` label precedence.\n\nConsequences observed:\n\n- `blocked` and `in_progress` BOTH map outbound to Jira \"In Progress\"\n  (non-injective forward map); `blocked` only round-trips via the\n  `rebar-status:blocked` annotation label.\n- The ONLY external control today is the `REBAR_RECONCILER_STATUS_GATING` env\n  gate — not a per-project mapping. `rebar.toml`'s `[reconciler]` section has\n  adapter/code-health keys but nothing for status mapping.\n- The inbound direction already accepts `\"Blocked\" -> blocked`; the outbound\n  direction still downgrades `blocked -> \"In Progress\"`.\n\n## Intent\n\nIntroduce a ONE-TIME, generic, provider-neutral, project-agnostic\n**status-map override** seam read from project configuration (e.g. a\n`[reconciler.status_map]` table in `rebar.toml`), with the current hardcoded\nmaps as the DEFAULT fallback. After this seam exists:\n\n- The REB \"Blocked\" change — and any future per-project workflow variance — is\n  expressed purely as project config data, never as a core edit.\n- Portability falls out for free: only a project that declares an override gets\n  it; projects whose workflow lacks a Blocked state keep today's behavior with\n  zero changes. No project-specific capability gating is added to core.\n\n## Scope / non-goals\n\n- IN scope: generic config-override machinery (parse, validate, merge over\n  defaults for both inbound and outbound directions), default-preserving\n  behavior, round-trip / parity test coverage, docs (`docs/config.md`,\n  reconciler mapping docs), and the `project.portability` plan-review\n  criterion.\n- OUT of scope: naming any specific project's states in core; changing the\n  default maps; the REB project's own `rebar.toml` values (that is downstream\n  project config once the seam lands).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Illegal-transition handling already exists at\n  `dispatch_one.py:402,445`; the override must interoperate with it.\n- Parity between the map copies is currently enforced by\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_config.py` — the seam must keep a single\n  source of truth or keep that parity green.\n\n**This epic is filed for future work and is intentionally out of scope for the\ncurrent session (no implementation here).**","id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Generic config-driven status-map override seam for per-project Jira workflow variance"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787159605255412001,"uuid":"d4374b74-bdec-47fc-9039-528f98f3a302"}